    "transcript": "A clear chart starts with one useful observation. First, check the market you are viewing, then choose a timeframe. Look for a price area you want to observe. Select H-Line and click once on the chart to mark it. Pause and check where the line landed. It records your observation; it does not guarantee that price will turn there. Return to Cursor when you finish drawing. For this first exercise, keep just one level on the chart. Open the chart exercise and explain why you chose that area.",
    "audio": "Arthur narration"
  },
